00:55:28.340 --> 00:55:41.400
Samuel Smith: Yeah, I just wanted… I just… I was concerned about that, because there are attacks on signatures that aren't… that… that have weaknesses that signatures bring with them that are… that make them weaker than normal hashes, in some ways.

416
00:55:41.400 --> 00:55:50.490
Daniel Hardman (Provenant, Inc.): Here was my reasoning, and… and this might be, an example of something that we want to discard because,

417
00:55:50.890 --> 00:56:06.499
Daniel Hardman (Provenant, Inc.): it kind of opens a door that might be dangerous, but my reasoning was, let's take W3C, we all know that, you know, JSON-LD transformations and signatures and whatever, there's a long, colorful history about

